.Dd October 1, 2026
.Dt SOCKET 2
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm socket ,
.Nm socketpair
.Nd create a socket, or a connected pair of sockets
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/socket.h
.Ft int
.Fn socket "int domain" "int type" "int protocol"
.Ft int
.Fn socketpair "int domain" "int type" "int protocol" "int sv[2]"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn socket
creates a socket and returns a descriptor open for reading and writing.
.Fa domain
selects the address family,
.Fa type
the socket type, and
.Fa protocol
the protocol where the type requires one.
.Pp
The supported combinations are:
.Bl -tag -width "AF_INET, SOCK_STREAM"
.It Dv AF_INET , SOCK_STREAM
A TCP stream socket.
.Fa protocol
is ignored.
.It Dv AF_INET , SOCK_DGRAM
A UDP datagram socket.
.Fa protocol
is ignored.
.It Dv AF_INET , SOCK_RAW
A raw ICMP socket when
.Fa protocol
is
.Dv IPPROTO_ICMP
(1).
.Dv IPPROTO_RAW
(255) creates a descriptor for network configuration ioctls only;
data operations return
.Er EOPNOTSUPP .
Other raw protocols are refused.
Effective user ID 0 is required for either raw form.
.It Dv AF_PACKET , SOCK_DGRAM
A packet socket.
Effective user ID 0 is required.
The low 16 bits of
.Fa protocol
must contain the Ethernet protocol in network byte order:
IPv4 (0x0800), ARP (0x0806), or zero.
Zero leaves the protocol unspecified until
.Xr bind 2 .
.It Dv AF_NETLINK , SOCK_RAW No or Dv SOCK_DGRAM
A netlink socket of protocol
.Dv NETLINK_ROUTE
(0), which answers requests for the machine's interfaces, addresses and
routes, or of
.Dv NETLINK_KOBJECT_UEVENT
(15), which hears nothing, as
.Xr netlink 7
describes.
.It Dv AF_UNIX , SOCK_STREAM , SOCK_DGRAM No or Dv SOCK_SEQPACKET
A socket between processes of this machine, described in
.Xr unix 7 .
.Fa protocol
must be 0 or
.Dv AF_UNIX
(1), as Linux takes it.
.Dv SOCK_RAW
is taken as
.Dv SOCK_DGRAM ,
as in Linux.
.El
.Pp
Other address families, including
.Dv AF_INET6 ,
are not supported.
.Pp
.Fn socketpair
makes two
.Dv AF_UNIX
sockets of
.Fa type
connected to each other and stores their descriptors in
.Fa sv ;
another domain fails with
.Er EOPNOTSUPP .
.Pp
.Fa type
may carry two creation flags above its low four bits, as Linux takes
them:
.Dv SOCK_CLOEXEC
sets the new descriptor's close-on-exec flag, and
.Dv SOCK_NONBLOCK
sets
.Dv O_NONBLOCK
on its open file description.
Any other bit above the low four gives
.Er EINVAL
before the family is looked at.
.Pp
Socket objects are allocated from the kernel heap, without a fixed pool
limit, and are freed when their last reference closes.
Descriptors duplicated by
.Xr dup 2
or inherited through
.Xr fork 2
refer to the same socket.
Descriptor allocation remains subject to the process's descriptor limit.
.Pp
The kernel interface is operation 1 of
.Xr socketcall 2
(i386 system call 102), whose argument block contains
.Fa domain , type ,
and
.Fa protocol
as three 32-bit words, or the direct call, number 359.
.Fn socketpair
is operation 8, with
.Fa sv
the fourth word, or number 360.
.Pp
On x86-64
.Nm socket
is call 41 and
.Nm socketpair
53, with no
.Nm socketcall .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn socket
returns a nonnegative descriptor on success.
On failure it returns -1 and sets
.Va errno .
The kernel operation returns a negative error number on failure.
.Sh EXAMPLES
The default suite's
.Pa tests/loopprobe.c
creates an
.Dv AF_INET , SOCK_DGRAM
socket with protocol 0, binds it, and sends and receives a datagram
through
.Li 127.0.0.1 .
.Pa tests/musl/sockflagmusl.c
creates sockets through operation 1 by number, with
.Dv SOCK_CLOEXEC
alone and with both flags, and checks the flags of each descriptor and
the
.Er EINVAL
of an unknown bit.
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width "[EPROTONOSUPPORT]"
.It Bq Er EAFNOSUPPORT
.Fa domain
is none of
.Dv AF_INET ,
.Dv AF_NETLINK ,
.Dv AF_PACKET
and
.Dv AF_UNIX .
.It Bq Er EFAULT
The socketcall argument block cannot be read.
.It Bq Er EINVAL
.Fa type
has a bit above its low four other than
.Dv SOCK_CLOEXEC
and
.Dv SOCK_NONBLOCK ,
the socket type is not accepted, or a packet protocol is neither zero,
IPv4, nor ARP.
An
.Dv AF_PACKET , SOCK_RAW
request also returns this error.
.It Bq Er EMFILE
The process has no free descriptor below its limit.
.It Bq Er ENOBUFS
The raw ICMP registration and receive queue cannot be allocated.
.It Bq Er ENOMEM
The socket object, a larger descriptor table or an open file description
cannot be allocated.
.It Bq Er EOPNOTSUPP
.Fn socketpair
was asked for a domain other than
.Dv AF_UNIX .
.It Bq Er EPERM
A raw IPv4 socket or packet socket was requested without effective user ID 0.
.It Bq Er EPROTONOSUPPORT
An IPv4 raw protocol is neither
.Dv IPPROTO_RAW
nor
.Dv IPPROTO_ICMP ,
an
.Dv AF_UNIX
protocol is neither 0 nor
.Dv AF_UNIX ,
or a netlink protocol is neither
.Dv NETLINK_ROUTE
nor
.Dv NETLINK_KOBJECT_UEVENT .
.It Bq Er ESOCKTNOSUPPORT
A privileged caller requested
.Dv AF_PACKET , SOCK_STREAM ,
an
.Dv AF_UNIX
type is not one of the three above, or a netlink type is neither
.Dv SOCK_RAW
nor
.Dv SOCK_DGRAM .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bind 2 ,
.Xr connect 2 ,
.Xr fcntl 2 ,
.Xr listen 2 ,
.Xr recv 2 ,
.Xr send 2 ,
.Xr socketcall 2 ,
.Xr netlink 7 ,
.Xr unix 7
